# Exact quantum ensemble bridge and its boundaries

This is a local, purely mathematical development until Q5 adopts a preparation interpretation. It proves a full reduced-state statement for a specified independent finite-level model. It is not a theorem for generic interacting quantum matter. Natural logarithms are used. Matrix entries and probabilities are dimensionless; energies are in joules, inverse energy parameters in J⁻¹, entropy after physical adoption in J K⁻¹. Finite-dimensional sums require no infinite product measure or choice axiom.

<a id="Q0"></a>
## Q0. Finite tensor states, subsystem restriction and trace tests

Let q≥1 be an integer and V=C^q with its standard inner product and orthonormal basis |j⟩, 1≤j≤q. The N-site Hilbert space V_N has the orthonormal basis |j_1,…,j_N⟩ indexed by {1,…,q}^N; its inner product is the sum of coordinate products. This is a concrete finite tensor product. A matrix ρ on V_N is a density matrix when ρ=ρ*, v*ρv≥0 for all v, and Trρ=1. An observable is a Hermitian matrix A; its expectation functional is TrρA. A positive measurement with r finite outcomes is a family M_a≥0 with Σ_a M_a=I; its outcome probabilities TrρM_a are nonnegative and sum to one, since TrρM_a=Tr(ρ^{1/2}M_aρ^{1/2})≥0 by diagonalizing the positive matrix ρ. Finite positive square roots are obtained by replacing each nonnegative eigenvalue by its square root.

The finite Hermitian diagonalization used here has a short complete proof. The unit sphere is compact by the actually read thermodynamics M32 bounded-sequence coordinate extraction argument. A Hermitian matrix A has real continuous Rayleigh function v*Av on that sphere, so a maximizing sequence has a convergent subsequence and a maximizer u. For every w perpendicular to u, differentiating the Rayleigh value of (u+tw)/||u+tw|| at real t=0 gives Re(w*Au)=0; replacing w by iw gives its imaginary part zero. Thus Au is perpendicular to u's orthogonal complement and Au=λu, λ=u*Au real. Hermiticity makes the complement invariant: u*Aw=(Au)*w=0. Induction on dimension gives an orthonormal eigenbasis. Positivity forces every eigenvalue nonnegative. This proves the required spectral and square-root interfaces without presupposing an infinite spectral theorem; the q=1 induction base is immediate.

Split N=k+(N−k) with 0≤k≤N, and write indices as (a,b). Define the reduced matrix (Tr_Bρ)_{a,a'}=Σ_b ρ_{(a,b),(a',b)}. It is Hermitian; for v in V_k,

v*Tr_Bρv=Σ_b (v⊗|b⟩)*ρ(v⊗|b⟩)≥0,

and its trace equals Trρ. For every matrix A on V_k, expansion of both finite traces gives Tr[(Tr_Bρ)A]=Tr[ρ(A⊗I)]. This also proves uniqueness of the reduced matrix because matrix units test every entry. A unitary change of environment basis leaves this formula unchanged: A⊗I is unchanged, and Tr(XY)=Tr(YX) follows by swapping the two finite summation indices. Thus restriction is an intrinsic subsystem state, not a choice of an environment coordinate distribution. A local observable is precisely A⊗I on a fixed k-site subsystem, with k independent of N when taking a thermodynamic limit.

For a Hermitian difference D with eigenvalues λ_i, define ||D||_1=Σ_i|λ_i|. If A is Hermitian with operator norm ≤1, then in an orthonormal eigenbasis of D,

|TrDA|=|Σ_iλ_i⟨u_i,Au_i⟩|≤Σ_i|λ_i|.

For diagonal D=diag(d_a), the trace norm is Σ_a|d_a|, so it equals twice total variation of the associated probability vectors, where TV(P,Q)=½Σ_a|P_a−Q_a|. In particular trace-norm convergence controls every bounded local quantum observable, including off-diagonal observables. For any effect 0≤M≤I and any Hermitian D of trace zero, diagonalizing D and writing D=D_+−D_- with TrD_+=TrD_-=||D||_1/2 gives |TrDM|≤||D||_1/2: both positive traces lie in [0,||D||_1/2]. Hence a fixed finite POVM has each outcome probability converging under this same bound. This statement concerns specified preparation probabilities, not observed frequencies or empirical evidence.

<a id="Q1"></a>
## Q1. Additive spectral Hamiltonian and its two ensembles

Choose real e_1,…,e_q, including repetitions to represent degeneracy. Define h|j⟩=e_j|j⟩ and H_N=Σ_{a=1}^N h^{(a)}, where h^{(a)} acts as h at the a-th factor and identity elsewhere. Thus H_N|j_1,…,j_N⟩=(Σ_a e_{j_a})|j_1,…,j_N⟩. A fixed one-site unitary U gives the equally covered h'=UhU*, H'_N=U^⊗N H_N(U*)^⊗N. No physical interaction is included; the site factorization is a specified model assumption if physically adopted.

Fix finite real β and set Z=Σ_j exp(−βe_j)>0, p_j=exp(−βe_j)/Z, E=Σ_jp_je_j. Positive-temperature adoption later restricts β>0; this finite algebra also permits β=0 and negative β. The finite Gibbs matrix γ=diag(p_j) is strictly positive. Matrix exponentiation is its convergent finite power series, or here direct diagonal exponentiation. Expansion in the product basis proves

exp(−βH_N)=⊗_{a=1}^N exp(−βh), Z_N=Z^N, γ_N=γ^⊗N.

For nonnegative widths δ_N define the spectral band projection Π_N by multiplying each product-basis vector by 1 when |Σ_ae_{j_a}−NE|≤δ_N and by 0 otherwise. It is an orthogonal projection, commutes with H_N, and its rank Ω_N counts all vectors in the band, not just distinct energy values. If Ω_N>0 define the microcanonical density σ_N=Π_N/Ω_N. This is the maximally mixed state on the specified spectral band. It is not a selected eigenvector, and degeneracies are included in the normalized trace. It is stationary under exp(−itH_N/ℏ) for any ℏ>0, as follows by the simultaneous diagonal entries; stationarity alone does not prove that an arbitrary initial state prepares it.

For a unitarily changed local energy basis, Π'_N=U^⊗NΠ_N(U*)^⊗N and σ'_N has the corresponding conjugation. Q0's expectation characterization gives Tr_Bσ'_N=U^⊗k(Tr_Bσ_N)(U*)^⊗k, since the environment unitary cancels under restriction. Trace norms of Hermitian differences are unchanged by this conjugation, which preserves their eigenvalues. All conclusions below therefore apply in every fixed local eigenbasis, including any rotation inside a degenerate eigenspace.

<a id="Q2"></a>
## Q2. Exact fixed-subsystem microcanonical/canonical equivalence

Assume δ_N/N→0 and δ_N≥C:=qΣ_j|e_j| for every N. This is the exact controlled-window hypothesis of the actually read thermodynamics L13. Its mathematical proof supplies the following finite combinatorial result: the uniform distribution on product labels satisfying the band constraint is nonempty, its fixed k-label marginal converges in total variation to p^⊗k, and logΩ_N/N→H(p):=−Σ_jp_jlogp_j. Its complete argument was read in `../../first-principles-2026-10-03/thermodynamics/scaffold/ly-closure-developments.md`, L13. For clarity, all steps needed for the transfer are restated here.

For a type n=(n_1,…,n_q), Σn_j=N, t_j=n_j/N, its multiplicity is N!/∏n_j!. The finite multinomial identity bounds it above by exp[NH(t)]. Increasing log and integration of log x bound log(m!) between ∫_1^m logx dx and ∫_1^{m+1}logx dx; evaluation gives log multiplicity=NH(t)+O_q(log(N+1)) uniformly, treating 0!=1. Round Np_j downward for j<q and place the remainder in the last count. Its total energy error is at most C, it converges to p, and therefore contributes exp[NH(p)−o(N)] vectors to the band. Nonemptiness for every N follows.

The Gibbs identity H(t)=H(p)+β(Σ_jt_je_j−E)−D(t||p) follows by inserting logp_j=−βe_j−logZ. The actually read finite KL inequality in thermodynamics M7 follows from logx≤x−1; equality only t=p. Consequently p uniquely maximizes H at exact mean E. The simplex is compact and H is continuous, including at zero because xlogx→0. For every ε>0 there is η>0 such that, when the mean tolerance is sufficiently small, every type with |t−p|≥ε has H(t)≤H(p)−η. Otherwise a convergent subsequence with mean error tending to zero and entropy approaching H(p) would violate uniqueness. There are at most (N+1)^q types. The multiplicity upper bound divided by the rounded-type lower bound shows that the uniform-band random type is outside any fixed ε with probability tending to zero exponentially.

Conditional on a type, its first k labels are sampled without replacement from the N positions. Couple independent uniform position sampling to distinct-position sampling: replace a repeated sampled position by a new uniform position among those not previously used. Until the first repetition both samples agree; by a union bound the chance of a repetition is ≤k(k−1)/(2N). Hence the total variation between the two ordered label laws is no larger than this number. The with-replacement law is t^⊗k. Type concentration and continuity of the finitely many products yield convergence to p^⊗k. Finally the lower bound above and the upper bound Ω_N≤(N+1)^q exp[N max_band H(t)] give logΩ_N/N→H(p), because compactness and the vanishing mean tolerance force max_band H(t)→H(p).

Now σ_N is diagonal, and Q0 restriction shows (σ_N)_k is diagonal with precisely the first k-label marginal. γ^⊗k is diagonal with p^⊗k. Therefore

||(σ_N)_k−γ^⊗k||_1=2 TV(label marginals)→0

for every fixed k. For every Hermitian k-site A, |Tr[(σ_N)_k−γ^⊗k]A|≤||A||·||(σ_N)_k−γ^⊗k||_1→0. This includes all coherences as observable tests: the two states' off-diagonal entries are exactly zero in this eigenbasis, rather than ignored in the notion of convergence. Their spectral entropies obey S(σ_N)=k_BlogΩ_N and S(γ_N)=Nk_BH(p), so their entropy difference divided by N tends to zero when entropy receives its physical normalization. The theorem does not say global trace norm tends to zero, permit k to grow with N, give arbitrary-band or exact-eigenenergy equivalence, or imply interacting quantum equivalence.

<a id="Q3"></a>
## Q3. Diagonal classical embeddings preserve full local quantum tests

For any finite set Λ of sites with the same q-state basis, let a classical probability P_Λ on {1,…,q}^Λ define D_Λ(P)=Σ_s P_Λ(s)|s⟩⟨s|. This is a positive trace-one matrix. If its probabilities are consistent under deleting sites, Q0's entry formula makes these matrices consistent. For an arbitrary matrix A on Λ,

Tr[D_Λ(P)A]=Σ_sP_Λ(s) A_{s,s}.

Thus consistency defines a linear normalized positive functional on the union of local matrix algebras: evaluate using any finite containing support, and positivity follows because positive matrices have nonnegative diagonal entries. It satisfies |ω(A)|≤||A||: the absolute diagonal entries are ≤||A|| and the probabilities sum to one. The union is normed by the matrix operator norm under A↦A⊗I, which preserves that norm (the upper inequality follows on decomposed environment coordinates, and testing v⊗b gives the lower one). Therefore it extends uniquely to its norm completion by taking limits of local approximants. Positivity persists because for any local-approximated X, ω(X*X) is a limit of nonnegative numbers, and every positive element can equivalently be defined as a norm limit of sums of such squares; the infinite worker supplies the full C*-algebra formulation. This construction does not identify a general quantum state with a probability on classical labels.

If finite P_n restrictions tend to P in total variation on each fixed Λ, then their diagonal quantum reduced matrices converge in trace norm on Λ by Q0. If instead a classical infinite-volume supplier gives convergence against every bounded measurable local function, the finitely many indicator functions of fixed Λ cylinder labels give the same conclusion. Hence the checked CSM finite-alphabet local ensemble or phase results can transfer to all fixed local matrix observables after this diagonal embedding. The physical Hamiltonian and preparation assumptions still need explicit adoption. In particular a continuum **positional** classical theorem does not supply a quantum kinetic-energy ensemble theorem. This elementary state embedding alone also does not prove KMS for noncommuting time evolution or prove that every quantum KMS state is diagonal; those are separate claims requiring the infinite worker's argument.

<a id="Q4"></a>
## Q4. Boundaries demonstrated by explicit normalized states

**Zero-width bands may be empty.** Take q=2, e_1=0,e_2=ε>0 J and βε=log√2. Then the canonical excited probability p_2=1/(1+√2) is irrational: if it were rational and nonzero, √2=1/p_2−1 would be rational, contrary to the elementary parity proof that a reduced rational square root of 2 would have both numerator and denominator even. Every H_N eigenvalue is an integer multiple of ε; Np_2 is irrational for every positive integer N. Thus the δ_N=0 band centered on the canonical mean is empty for every N. A normalized σ_N does not exist in this model. The controlled width in Q2 is a substantive assumption.

**Entropy density does not force a fixed subsystem.** For q=2 and γ=I/2, define τ_N=|1⟩⟨1|⊗(I/2)^⊗(N−1). Its eigenvalues are 2^{−(N−1)} with multiplicity 2^{N−1} plus zeros, so S(τ_N)=(N−1)k_Blog2 while S(γ_N)=Nk_Blog2. The entropy difference per site tends to zero, but ||(τ_N)_1−I/2||_1=1 for every N. This inhomogeneous preparation establishes why entropy-density comparison alone is insufficient.

**All fixed blocks need not give global trace norm.** For N≥2, let π_N be uniform on binary product labels of even parity. There are 2^{N−1} such labels. For any k<N fixed labels, exactly 2^{N−k−1} completions have the required parity, so (π_N)_k=I/2^k. Nevertheless π_N has diagonal entries 2^{−(N−1)} on even labels and zero on odd labels, whereas γ_N=I/2^N on both. Summing absolute differences gives ||π_N−γ_N||_1=1. The global parity effect distinguishes them with probability difference 1/2. These are hypothetical preparation counterexamples, not evidence that a laboratory prepares such states or an additive energy-shell example.

<a id="Q5"></a>
## Q5. Physical preparation interface and primitive quantities

Adopt the already explicit NRQM density/Born preparation interface, independently of its equilibrium interpretation: a system assigned a Hilbert space and a density operator has probabilities TrρM_a for the specified POVM. The Hamiltonian h is the primitive model's energy observable, with measured/assigned energy parameters e_j in J; the tensor factorization identifies separately addressable noninteracting sites. A canonical preparation assigns exp(−βH_N)/Tr exp(−βH_N), and a band preparation assigns Π_N/TrΠ_N when the stated band is nonempty. These are alternative adopted preparations; unitary stationarity and mathematical maximum entropy do not derive equilibration or apparatus behavior. β is the inverse-energy preparation parameter; identifying β=1/(k_BT) uses the explicit thermal bridge, k_B>0 in J K⁻¹, T>0 in K. ℏ>0 in J s sets unitary dynamical phase and is absent from the finite normalization calculation. State entropy S=−k_BTrρlogρ is derived from the spectral eigenvalue sum, with 0log0=0. Site number is a dimensionless integer; no volume/pressure/density is implicit until a lattice spacing/geometry and volume convention is specified. Degeneracy counts are dimensionless. β<0 is only the covered bounded-spectrum mathematical family unless a separate bounded-energy physical preparation is adopted.

Under these preparations Q2 is a conditional physical theorem: every fixed subsystem's measurement probabilities converge, and the stated entropy density agrees. Q4 supplies proved hypothetical counterexamples to stronger interpretations. Nothing here uses empirical observations as a premise, and no result says observed finite frequencies equal their probabilities. If a finite number of repeated preparations is used to estimate these probabilities, independence, detector calibration, resolution and statistical uncertainty must be separately specified.

<a id="Q6"></a>
## Q6. Interacting finite-regulator trace-Gibbs interface

There is a genuine interacting infinite-dimensional normal-state branch beyond occupation products. The stable QFT supplier `thm-qft-regulated-gibbs-trace` has its actually read complete argument at `../quantum-field-theory/workers/interactions-renormalization/proofs.md#ir02`, with the necessary IR00–IR01 form construction also read. Fix a finite positive number r of real modes, Hilbert space L²(R^r,dq), dimensionless coordinates q, a_j>0, and a real polynomial V(q)≥c|q|²−C₀ with c>0,C₀≥0. Complete C_c∞ in the form norm

a(u,u)=Σ_j a_j||∂_ju||²+∫(V+C₀+2)|u|².

The supplier proves this completion embeds densely, injectively and compactly in L²: weak derivative/weighted limits establish injectivity; the explicit cube-mean Poincaré bound and coercive tails give finite-dimensional approximants. Riesz representation then constructs the compact positive injective inverse R of the form operator plus identity. Its eigenvectors ψ_n form a complete orthonormal family, μ_n>0, and the self-adjoint operator h_W has eigenvalues E_n=μ_n⁻¹−1 on its precise domain ΣE_n²|c_n|²<∞. The desired h=h_W−(C₀+1)I extends −Σ_j a_j∂_j²+V on compact smooth functions. The assertion is about this selected form realization; it does not identify its domain with a separately unproved maximal differential domain or assert essential self-adjointness of C_c∞.

The supplier also proves a spectral comparison, rather than assuming that compact resolvent implies summable Gibbs weights. The oscillator form with c|q|² is bounded above by the h_W form. Among the first k h_W eigenvectors a finite linear-system argument gives a unit vector perpendicular to the first k−1 oscillator eigenvectors. Its form energy is simultaneously ≤E_k and ≥E_osc,k, where E_osc,n=Σ_j√(a_jc)(2n_j+1). Thus E_k≥E_osc,k, and the Gibbs sum is bounded by the product of r convergent oscillator geometric sums. This proves trace-class exp(−b h) for every b>0, after the finite energy shift. All finite physical β intervals therefore satisfy the finite-state worker's trace-Gibbs theorem hypotheses.

Assign an energy scale E_*>0 J and H=E_*h. For every β>0 J⁻¹ the exact Gibbs density is exp(−βH)/Z with finite Z, and every normal competitor of finite form energy has finite entropy and satisfies the unique Gibbs free-energy inequality by `thm-qsm-trace-gibbs-variational`. The argument is literal hypothesis substitution: b=βE_*>0; H is self-adjoint bounded below, its exponential is trace class on (0,∞), and finite-form-energy competitors have finite cross-log entropy. No diagonal restriction on the competitors is imposed, and no Gibbs formula for a nontrace-class continuum system is used.

A concrete interacting choice is V=½m₀²Σq_j²+½J₀Σ_links(q_i−q_j)²+λΣq_j⁴, with finite graph, m₀>0,J₀≥0,λ>0 dimensionless rescaled couplings. It has c=m₀²/2,C₀=0 and the above hypotheses. These are regulator/model parameters; m₀ is not automatically the kilogram particle mass, q_j not automatically a meter position, and coordinate conjugates not automatically mechanical momenta. Physical interpretation adopts this fixed regulated quantum Hamiltonian and canonical preparation. The resulting bounded-observable probabilities and finite-form free-energy inequality are conditional predictions. Removal of the regulator, an infinite-mode interacting Gibbs trace, a general infinite-volume KMS construction, a four-dimensional continuum interacting QFT or a macroscopic phase theorem do not follow from this branch.
